            <ArticleTitle>[Symptomatic Intraosseous Ganglion of the Trapezium. Case Report and Literature Review].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>279-282</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An intraosseous ganglion cyst has been reported in nearly all of the carpal bones; it is a rare cause of chronic wrist pain. The case presented here is a rare finding of symptomatic intraosseous ganglion of the trapezium bone. The relevant literature is reviewed. Key words: ganglion cyst, trapezium bone, wrist.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
